## Context

`make slides` fails with `No rule to make target '…fig_capability_dag.pdf'`.
The 0365 docs-build workflow lands with `continue-on-error: true` on the
slides step until this is fixed; 0358's required-checks flip (which now
includes `docs-build` per user direction) cannot complete until this is
green.

The mismatch:

- Root `Makefile:215-227` `slides/slides.pdf` rule lists
  `$(GEN)/fig_capability_timeline.pdf` as a prereq but **not**
  `$(GEN)/fig_capability_dag.pdf`.
- `slides/Makefile:16,29-30` consumes both
  `fig_capability_timeline.pdf` (twice) and `fig_capability_dag.pdf`.
- The recursive sub-make cannot resolve `fig_capability_dag.pdf`
  because the root never builds it for the slides path. The root
  Makefile *does* have a rule (`Makefile:190`), but the rule only
  fires if something declares the file as a prereq.

The DAG guard (0363) does not catch this — recursive-make visibility
is its known limit.

## Relevant files

- `Makefile:215-227` — `slides/slides.pdf` prereq list (needs the addition).
- `Makefile:190` — `fig_capability_dag.pdf` rule (already exists; correct).
- `slides/Makefile:16,29-30` — consumer side (already references both).
- `tests/test_makefile_dag.py` (or equivalent) — DAG guard; verify it now sees the link.

## Actions

1. Add `$(GEN)/fig_capability_dag.pdf` to the `slides/slides.pdf` prereq list in `Makefile` (after line 220 `fig_capability_timeline.pdf`).
2. Run `make slides` locally if an engine is available; otherwise rely on `make -n slides | grep fig_capability_dag` to confirm the prereq is visible.
3. Confirm `tests/test_makefile_dag.py` (or whichever DAG guard exists) still passes — and ideally tightens its visibility into this case.

## Test

First failing test (TDD red): `make -n slides | grep -F 'fig_capability_dag.pdf'` returns at least one hit at the root-make level (currently zero). After the fix, it returns at least one. Wrap as a pytest adherence test if not already covered.

## Verification

- [ ] `make -n slides | grep -F 'fig_capability_dag.pdf'` shows the prereq.
- [ ] `make slides` succeeds on an engine-equipped host (or the docs-build workflow from 0365 reports a green slides step).
- [ ] `make check` still passes.

## Invariants

- The existing DAG/Makefile adherence tests do not regress.
- `fig_capability_timeline.pdf` remains a prereq (don't replace, add).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `Makefile` `slides/slides.pdf` rule lists both `fig_capability_timeline.pdf` and `fig_capability_dag.pdf` as prereqs.
- [ ] `make -n slides` references both figures.
- [ ] `make check` green.

